<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error. It is also why there is no <description>: no quick
         action in this repo carries one (0 of 80 measured), QuickAction.Description is capped at
         255 characters, and a comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API.

         ADDED 2026-08-27 (finishes commit a939e97, 2026-08-26, which did this job for the
         DISPOSITION side of NDA__c/LOI__c/Contract_Review__c and deliberately left the
         ACQUISITION side on the generic Advance Stage button). User decision, restated for the
         acquisition side: "we don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage'; instead we need
         the NEXT STAGE NAME." One headless action per acquisition hop of NDA__c.Status__c,
         labelled with the stage the click lands on.

         THE HOP: NDA acquisition sequence is Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent ('Sent' is
         terminal). This action serves Pending -> Received, gated on
         {!Record.Status__c} EQUAL 'Pending' on NDA_Record_Page.

         🔴 THE LABEL IS THE ONLY THING THAT DIFFERS BETWEEN THESE ACTIONS. This action points at
         the SAME c/advanceRecordStage bundle as NDA__c.Advance_Stage, NDA__c.Move_to_Signed and
         NDA__c.Move_to_Sent; that component names no object and holds no stage map -
         RecordStageAdvanceService derives the target from the record's CURRENT stage via
         CONFIG_BY_TYPE, keyed per RECORD TYPE, and advance() takes only a recordId. The label is
         therefore a promise the page's visibility rule keeps, not anything the client sends, and
         the two must be kept in step by hand.

         🔴 RECORD-TYPE POLARITY - NDA_Record_Page gates this entry with
         {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} NE 'Disposition_NDA' (NOT EQUAL 'Acquisition_NDA').
         NE fails OPEN on a Master/blank-typed row (blank NE 'Disposition_NDA' is TRUE), which
         MATCHES RecordStageAdvanceService - its defaultTypeKey routes a Master row to the
         ACQUISITION map. EQUAL 'Acquisition_NDA' would fail CLOSED and strand every Master-typed
         row with no button while the server would happily have advanced it. Same polarity
         NDA_Record_Page's header already documents for the disposition side, applied here in the
         opposite direction.

         ACQUISITION_NDA'S OWN Advance_Stage ENTRY IS REMOVED, NOT LEFT ALONE, in this same
         change - unlike a939e97's disposition-side edit, which added criteria to Advance_Stage
         and left it in place. This wave replaces both acquisition Advance_Stage entries
         (live-gated and the already-dead disposition-gated one a939e97 explicitly left for "a
         separate, deliberate step") with named per-hop buttons on both sides of this object. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Received</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
